  "reviewNotes": [
    "The current 2026 recommendation explicitly provides the 4-item CDS table and the 0 / 1-4 / 5-8 interpretation.",
    "The source groups scores 5-8 as moderate and severe dehydration without giving a split point; MiniMed must not invent separate moderate/severe cutoffs.",
    "CDS does not by itself calculate percent fluid deficit or a rehydration volume.",
    "Original validation was in children with acute gastroenteritis; the 2026 ARVI recommendation uses CDS when dehydration assessment is needed in the ARVI context.",
    "Promotion to a runtime tool requires rights review, population wording and UX review."
